text='# PFP prompts 32 through 51\n\nTwenty previously unrun prompts were executed locally through P0/P1/P2/P4/P5, with P3 only for actual failed native gates. Each run and review retains operad deltas, exact source snapshots, full native cross-language outputs and literal named kernel reports. This is one local Codex researcher, not an independent-author panel or external-provider transcript.\n\n| Prompt | Supported step | Remaining obligation |\n|---|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join(table)+'\n\nThe review distinguishes exact retained finite computations from universal proofs and physical or continuum imports. The Bell-input carrier was also corrected to rank at most one: the retained zero-scale control has rank zero, and negativity requires positive scale. Specific repairs/fences include: actual three-split path overcount instead of a two-term arithmetic proxy; compatibility without a claimed convergence certificate; Euler drift despite zero instantaneous squared-mass rate; class completeness versus Kraus completeness; all-rational polynomial-root exclusion instead of four-candidate testing; rejection of the fake 9/4 embedding with residual 1/16; and a genuine Bell partial-transpose negative witness in place of CP/Stinespring declaration flags. All captured prompts, source labels and original stage bytes remain sealed. The concurrent upstream naming migration is preserved in canonical prompt/operad paths; upstream baseline Git blobs and the unchanged mathematical statements are verified separately. Formal coordinate/matrix transports and full refined-carrier operad identity, substitution, symmetry and coherence remain open where stated.\n\nMeasured counts: '+json.dumps(counts,sort_keys=True)+'.\n\nFresh integration: '+json.dumps(integration,sort_keys=True)+'. Counts are unique tests and anchors, not sums of repeated gates. Retained failed checkpoints are included in the measured count and never promoted to passing. Pinned cached Mathlib is an import; no fresh full Mathlib build, full transitive dependency custody, whole-repository/hosted CI or completed physical reconstruction is claimed.\n\nRead-only exact/custody replay (checks saved compiler receipts and recomputes exact predicates):\n\n    py -3.9 -X utf8 verify_batch.py\n    py -3.9 -X utf8 -O verify_batch.py\n    py -3.9 -X utf8 test_custody_guards.py -v\n\nA concurrent upstream merge changed path naming and enhanced E003/E005. The batch preserves the incoming canonical metadata and root list, retains its exact earlier source versions, and rebuilds all 33 required local Lean modules on the integrated tree. The full corpus validator and protocol suite retain incoming upstream failures; exact upstream/current comparisons are recorded instead of claiming they pass. Earlier failed integration gates, including an incomplete baseline checkout that was rejected and repaired, remain saved. Passing native compiler receipts are reused only after all their recorded source digests are rechecked. The single root-list conflict retained PromptDynamics and each upstream foundation module once. upstream/ stores the pinned base, Git-blob baselines and reconciliation receipt.\n\nDedicated per-prompt README and scope_review.json files state the supported step and remaining obligations. Construction, review, native receipts and Git staging tools are retained here. Source digests bind bytes, not independent authorship. External provider calls: zero; chat cost unmeasured. GitHub merge state is verified separately. AuthorityEffect: None.\n'

